      <h2>The Flaw with Traditional Lead Forms in 2026</h2>
      <p>Instant forms rely on Meta's autofill data. When users tap an ad, Facebook pre-fills their email and phone number from when they registered their profile—often 5 to 10 years ago. When sales agents dial the number, they encounter:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Disconnected lines or outdated secondary SIM cards.</li>
        <li>Aggressive call spam filters (Truecaller, Apple Silence Unknown Callers).</li>
        <li>Procrastination and friction: By the time a rep calls, the user has forgotten submitting the form.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why Click-to-WhatsApp Dominates High-Intent Niches</h2>
      <p>For real estate brokers, cosmetic clinics, car dealerships, course creators, and boutique agencies, WhatsApp bypasses phone tag entirely:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Zero Spam Numbers:</strong> Because the user must initiate the conversation inside WhatsApp, their active phone number is guaranteed.</li>
        <li><strong>Frictionless Qualification:</strong> Automated greeting messages and chatbots can ask 3 qualifying questions (budget, timeline, location) before routing to a senior closer.</li>
        <li><strong>Media Sharing:</strong> Reps can instantly send brochures, video walkthroughs, and audio notes inside the chat without waiting for an email reply.</li>
      </ol>

